// Two spellings of one identifier, refused as a duplicate.
//
// Parse stage: the module hooks each global name as it is parsed, so the
// collision is reported before any analysis runs. lexical_tokens establishes
// that back-ticks admit characters an identifier could not otherwise hold;
// what they do not do is make a new name. The lexer interns the characters
// between them, so `abc` and abc are one spelling, and two declarations of it
// collide as any two do. core_parse_names owns the duplicate rule; this file
// owns only that the ticks are no part of the spelling.

mod lexical_reject_spelling;

var @threadlocal abc = 1;            //~ ErrorDupName:18 "This is the conflicting definition for that name" follow-on
var @threadlocal `abc` = 2;          //~ ErrorDupName:18 "Global name is already defined"
